<title>BELGIUM: EU to vet NEC /Bull joint venture.</title>
<headline>EU to vet NEC /Bull joint venture.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Friday it would examine plans by NEC, Compagnie des Machines Bull SA and Packard Bell Electronics to form a joint venture.</p>
<p>In a statement, the European Union executive said the companies had notified the deal on January 21. The Commission said it could fall within the scope of EU rules which ban anti-competitive agreements. There are no deadlines for these kind of investigations.</p>
<p>Bull and NEC have each acquired a minority stake in Packard Bell Electronics, which now is called Packard Bell NEC (PB). NEC holds about 44 percent of the total share capital and Bull between 16 and 26 percent.</p>
<p>In addition, Bull has sold to PB the whole of the issued share capital of its personal computer business, while NEC has transferred to PB certain assets of its worldwide PC business.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom +32 2 287 68 11</p>
